{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Enough, etc., and was left over.</b> These are two contradictory things: if it was enough, there was nothing left over, and if there was left over, it was not enough. And here there is no room to say 'not only this but also that,' since both are one category and one aspect, and it is not the way to make one category into two categories, for in what is heard there is a contradiction. Further, there was no need to say 'enough' but rather 'and the work was left over for all the work.' Further, the entire verse is superfluous, for it says above 'the people were bringing more than enough for the work,' and it is obvious that they did not say so until they estimated, so what need is there further to say 'and the work' etc.?" "Or perhaps the verse informs us of the belovedness of the children of Israel in the eyes of the Place (HaMakom), for since Israel brought more than the required measure, HaShem was scrupulous about the honor of every person who took trouble and brought, and everything brought entered the House of HaShem within the work of the Mishkan. And this is the measure of the verse: <b>and the work</b> that YHWH commanded to make for the Mishkan sufficed to absorb within it all the work that the children of Israel did — even the surplus, meaning what was more than necessary: the receptacle sufficed to receive more than its measure by way of a miracle. Or on this reading, <b>and the work</b> that they brought <b>was enough</b> — neither lacking nor excessive, even though in truth it was more, as He says <b>and was left over</b>, for a miracle was performed and nothing was left over."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:37:07.243594863Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}